---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Portrait from '../components/Portrait.astro';
import FillIn from '../components/FillIn.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import portrait from '../assets/portrait-extended.png';
import { site } from '../site';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Who Alex Finnarn is: twelve years of Drupal platforms, testing and community organizing, and the principles he works by."
>
  <div class="container patch page">
    <PageHeader title="About">
      <p>
          When the old gatekeepers stop vouching for people, how do you decide who to trust?
      </p>
    </PageHeader>
    <div class="intro section">
      <Portrait src={portrait} alt={`Colored-pencil drawing of ${site.name}`} />
      <div class="prose measure">
        <p>
          I've been building websites since about 2013. The first one was my own Drupal 7 blog, and I
          spent way too much time rounding the corners of its header.
        </p>
        <p>
          For the next twelve years or so, Drupal was the job. I started out fixing bugs and making
          small feature updates, and worked my way up to running whole applications, including being
          the one who brought the service back up when it went down. One of them was a Drupal service
          running more than 800 sites for thousands of content editors.
        </p>
        <p>
          Along the way I picked up the jobs nobody else wanted. As a junior dev I took over my team's
          test suite, mostly because no one else wanted to eat their vegetables, and cut the Behat run
          time by about 60%. I've given talks on testing, including one on Cypress at DrupalCamp NJ in
          2023, and left hundreds of comments in Drupal's issue queues.
        </p>
        <p>
          I also like getting people in a room. I revived the ReactJS Columbus meetup in 2020 and helped
          organize community conferences. Judging by the number of groups I've seen die, I'm better at
          the talking than the organizing.
        </p>
        <p>
          In late 2024 I quit federal contract work. These days I build AI-assisted workflows on a
          $20-a-month plan, because I think regular people should get to use them too.
        </p>
        <FillIn what="Bio: the move into a new industry, framed as a strength (docs/interview.md, questions 11–13)." />
      </div>
    </div>
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Principles</h2>
      <ul class="principles">
        <li>
          <h3>Pursue the truth</h3>
          <p>I'd rather tell you what something really costs than sell you on "free."</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Mix it up</h3>
          <p>The useful connections usually come from a field I wasn't supposed to be looking at.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Build ritual</h3>
          <p>Good work comes from daily habits more than bursts of inspiration.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Start from first principles</h3>
          <p>Before anyone writes code, I want to know what the thing is actually for.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Keep it explainable</h3>
          <p>If you can't explain a workflow in plain language, it's too complex to build.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Intent over implementation</h3>
          <p>Decide what a page should achieve before arguing about how it looks.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Own your content</h3>
          <p>Your words, and how you manage them, should outlive whatever tool publishes them.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <div class="actions">
      <Button href="/contact/">Contact</Button>
      <Button href="/work/" variant="secondary">Work</Button>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .intro {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(14rem, 26rem) 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .prose > :global(* + *) {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
  }

  .principles {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-5);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .principles h3 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .principles p {
    margin: var(--space-1) 0 0;
  }

  .actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    padding-block: var(--space-6) var(--space-section);
  }

  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .intro {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
